{"beat": 28, "name": "WHAT THE DIME TAUGHT", "text": "So test the moral. Find a price that works and hold it. The dime was brilliant: an advertisement, a discipline on cost, a promise a customer could remember. But the moral is missing a piece. A price that never moves can't tell you what a different price would do. Woolworth knew, to the fraction of a cent, what a gross of soap cost him. What he couldn't know, from inside a ceiling, was what his customers would have paid above it. For decades the company learned a great deal about the cost side of its price, and far less about the demand side, because the demand side only speaks when the price moves. When it finally listened, it did it by testing. And then it promised the new ceiling would hold. A price that's tested once and then held for decades isn't a measurement anymore. It's a memory.", "provider": "placeholder", "words": [{"word": "So", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.18}, {"word": "test", "start": 0.18, "end": 0.48}, {"word": "the", "start": 0.48, "end": 0.68}, {"word": "moral.", "start": 0.68, "end": 0.98}, {"word": "Find", "start": 1.54, "end": 1.7}, {"word": "a", "start": 1.7, "end": 1.84}, {"word": "price", "start": 1.84, "end": 2.06}, {"word": "that", "start": 2.06, "end": 2.26}, {"word": "works", "start": 2.26, "end": 2.58}, {"word": "and", "start": 2.58, "end": 2.76}, {"word": "hold", "start": 2.76, "end": 3.06}, {"word": "it.", "start": 3.06, "end": 3.22}, {"word": "The", "start": 3.68, "end": 3.78}, {"word": "dime", "start": 3.78, "end": 4.12}, {"word": "was", "start": 4.12, "end": 4.36}, {"word": "brilliant:", "start": 4.36, "end": 4.76}, {"word": "an", "start": 5.28, "end": 5.4}, {"word": "advertisement,", "start": 5.4, "end": 6.0}, {"word": "a", "start": 6.46, "end": 6.52}, {"word": "discipline", "start": 6.52, "end": 6.88}, {"word": "on", "start": 6.88, "end": 7.18}, {"word": "cost,", "start": 7.18, "end": 7.6}, {"word": "a", "start": 7.86, "end": 7.96}, {"word": "promise", "start": 7.96, "end": 8.28}, 